{# gfadmin/templates/admin/form.html, rendered with page_title "New Need"
   (gfadmin/views.py:1922) -- the create half of Django's one need_form
   view. admin/need_form.njk in this same directory is the edit half; the
   two are separate templates here only because they were built in
   different work packages, and the follow-up that merges them is in the
   WP 6.8 wiring notes. Field NAMES are identical in both, so one POST
   handler could serve both the moment they merge.

   Bulma classes are copied from what django-bulma's `{{ form|bulma }}`
   filter emits for each widget type (div.field > label.label >
   div.control > .input/.textarea/.checkbox), rather than from the Django
   template, which only ever writes the filter.

   FIXES admin/form.html:31-37's dead food-bank preview (defect D2):
   views.py:1926-1928 resolves `foodbank` from `?foodbank=` and then never
   puts it in template_vars (1941-1945), so the second column that block
   was written for has never rendered on this page in production. Restored
   here -- through the port's own safe proxy signature
   (`?foodbank=<slug>&field=<known field>`, routes/admin/proxy.ts), never
   Django's raw `?url=` SSRF that WP 6.3 already replaced.
   `field=url` is the food bank's own website, matching what
   admin/form.html:33 asked for (`{{ foodbank.url|urlencode }}`). #}
{% extends "admin/page.njk" %}

{% block title %}{{ page_title }}{% endblock %}

{% block body %}
<div class="columns">
  <div class="column is-half">
    <h1 class="title">{{ page_title }}</h1>
    {% if form.foodbank_slug %}
      <p><a href="/admin/foodbank/{{ form.foodbank_slug }}/">&larr; Back</a></p>
    {% endif %}

    {% if error %}
      <div class="notification is-danger is-light">{{ error }}</div>
    {% endif %}

    <form method="post" action="">
      <input type="hidden" name="csrf_token" value="{{ csrf_token }}">

      {# givefood/forms.py:232 -- `foodbank = ModelChoiceField(queryset=
         Foodbank.objects.filter().order_by('name'))`, i.e. a <select> the
         admin picks by NAME. A bare slug box meant anyone arriving here
         without a `?foodbank=` seed had to already know the exact slug, and
         a typo only surfaced as an error after submitting. Still a text
         input rather than Django's <select> -- that queryset is unscoped
         (~1,000+ options, open and closed alike) and a `?foodbank=` seed has
         to survive even for a food bank the list does not carry -- but now
         backed by a datalist of name -> slug pairs, so the food bank is once
         again selectable by the name the caller gives on the phone. The list
         holds OPEN food banks only (getOpenFoodbankOptions); a closed one is
         still reachable by typing its slug, which is exactly why this stays
         free text and not a <select>. #}
      <div class="field">
        <label class="label" for="id_foodbank">Food Bank Slug</label>
        <div class="control">
          <input class="input" type="text" id="id_foodbank" name="foodbank_slug" value="{{ form.foodbank_slug }}" placeholder="(none)" list="foodbank_slugs" autocomplete="off">
          <datalist id="foodbank_slugs">
            {% for option in foodbank_options %}
            <option value="{{ option.slug }}">{{ option.name }}</option>
            {% endfor %}
          </datalist>
        </div>
        <p class="help">Start typing a food bank&rsquo;s name to pick it from the list. Leave blank to leave this need unassigned to any food bank. A need cannot be published without one.</p>
      </div>

      {# Labels are the model's explicit verbose_names (givefood/models/needs.py:64
         "Shopping List" and :67 "Excess Items"), which is what bulma/forms/
         field.html renders as `{{ field.label }}`.

         The two ids are load-bearing, not cosmetic: static/js/admin.js:103-104
         selects these textareas as `#id_change_text` / `#id_excess_change_text`
         and initChangeTextButtons() (admin.js:408-409) returns at its first
         line when the first is missing, so without them the "Make Titlecase",
         "CSV to Lines" and "Find & Replace" buttons are never injected. Same
         rule as includes/formfields.njk:5-14.

         `required` matches needs.py:64: change_text has no blank=True, so
         NeedForm builds a required field. Server-side check in needNew.ts. #}
      <div class="field">
        <label class="label" for="id_change_text">Shopping List</label>
        <div class="control">
          <textarea class="textarea" id="id_change_text" name="change_text" rows="6" required>{{ form.change_text }}</textarea>
        </div>
        <p class="help">One item per line.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="field">
        <label class="label" for="id_excess_change_text">Excess Items</label>
        <div class="control">
          <textarea class="textarea" id="id_excess_change_text" name="excess_change_text" rows="6">{{ form.excess_change_text }}</textarea>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="field">
        <div class="control">
          <label class="checkbox"><input type="checkbox" name="published" value="1"{% if form.published %} checked{% endif %}> Published</label>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="field">
        <div class="control">
          <button type="submit" class="button is-link is-light" onclick="this.form.submit();this.disabled = true;">Save</button>
        </div>
      </div>
    </form>
  </div>

  {% if show_preview %}
    <div class="column is-half">
      <iframe class="preview-frame" src="/admin/proxy/?foodbank={{ form.foodbank_slug }}&amp;field=url" style="width:100%;height:1000px;border:none;" loading="lazy"></iframe>
    </div>
  {% endif %}
</div>
{% endblock %}
